1
00:00:04,330 --> 00:00:06,133
Once you have a
few notes, finding

2
00:00:06,165 --> 00:00:07,935
the right one should
take a second.

3
00:00:08,010 --> 00:00:08,751
Here's how.

4
00:00:09,901 --> 00:00:12,031
Press Command K,
or click Search,

5
00:00:12,241 --> 00:00:13,661
to open the command palette.

6
00:00:14,897 --> 00:00:16,167
Before you type anything,

7
00:00:16,407 --> 00:00:18,027
it lists your most recent notes.

8
00:00:19,098 --> 00:00:19,918
Type any word.

9
00:00:20,318 --> 00:00:21,708
Tidepool searches titles,

10
00:00:21,818 --> 00:00:23,225
text and tags at once.

11
00:00:24,705 --> 00:00:25,975
Matches are highlighted,

12
00:00:26,215 --> 00:00:27,685
and the best one comes first.

13
00:00:28,633 --> 00:00:30,753
Use the arrow keys
to choose a result,

14
00:00:31,003 --> 00:00:32,585
then press Enter to open it.

15
00:00:34,965 --> 00:00:36,215
Start with a hash sign,

16
00:00:36,485 --> 00:00:38,505
and the palette lists
your tags instead.

17
00:00:39,844 --> 00:00:41,458
Press Enter, and the list shows

18
00:00:41,524 --> 00:00:42,994
only the notes with that tag.

19
00:00:44,344 --> 00:00:45,554
With the list in focus,

20
00:00:45,674 --> 00:00:47,434
J and K step through the notes.

21
00:00:47,834 --> 00:00:48,879
No mouse needed.

22
00:00:50,849 --> 00:00:51,919
To narrow it further,

23
00:00:52,036 --> 00:00:53,479
type in Filter this list.

24
00:00:53,879 --> 00:00:55,107
Escape clears it again.

25
00:00:56,797 --> 00:00:58,147
The sidebar works too.

26
00:00:58,557 --> 00:00:59,983
Click any notebook or tag

27
00:01:00,032 --> 00:01:01,315
to filter with one click.

28
00:01:03,325 --> 00:01:05,047
Finally, a greater-than sign

29
00:01:05,100 --> 00:01:06,525
turns search into commands.

30
00:01:06,955 --> 00:01:08,200
Let's try dark mode.

31
00:01:10,771 --> 00:01:12,417
Every note, tag and command

32
00:01:12,464 --> 00:01:13,720
is one shortcut away.

33
00:01:14,920 --> 00:01:17,110
So: Command K
searches everything,

34
00:01:17,420 --> 00:01:18,900
a hash jumps to tags,

35
00:01:19,150 --> 00:01:20,757
and greater-than runs commands.

36
00:01:22,557 --> 00:01:24,127
Your notes stay on your device,

37
00:01:24,317 --> 00:01:25,787
and now they're easy to find.
